 failure the operator must see'","The plan uses no explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) for the provider-raises arm; it collapses all provider failures to a single exit-1-with-reason outcome."],"finding":"The handler maps a provider that raises (status `unavailable` / exception) to exit 1 carrying `reason`, but never states the DISPOSITION of that arm — whether a provider failure is retryable/transient (e.g. a 429 throttle, a timeout) versus fatal/permanent (e.g. an auth denial). The operator sees exit 1 and a reason string either way, with no disposition distinction to tell them whether re-running could succeed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f05da3cf2b15278ff","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design step 1 and AC 'An embedding provider that raises exits 1 and the message carries the failure reason.'","norm_id":"nc8841df106cb9a24","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient provider throttle (429) and a permanent auth failure both surface as exit 1 with a reason string; an operator or wrapping script cannot distinguish a case worth retrying from a fatal misconfiguration without parsing the free-text reason."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irre